{"c":[{"id":"594740d627151f97","sum":"HNSW, for any later re-add (2026-10-21, DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0): deleting embeddings rows with the index up leaks one index copy at checkpoint or process close; a no-match delete does not. Drop index, delete, recreate, checkpoint keeps used blocks flat.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T200533Z-dc75d974ecb1c63f","text":"2026-10-21: deleting embeddings rows with the HNSW index up leaks one index copy at checkpoint or process close, on DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. A no-match delete does not. The drop covers those deletes, not only inserts.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T202433Z-25b36bcacf2f9117","text":"2026-10-21 eleventh L4 preflight PASS WITH ADVISORY. Drop, delete, recreate, checkpoint keeps HNSW used blocks flat on DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. Advisories unadopted: checkpoint while the index is down; ingest keeps the index down for the whole process.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"a03e92dc6ad2d6f7","sum":"HNSW write rules, for any later re-add (operator 2026-10-21): keep the index down until every embedding delete in the process has run, then recreate once (a recreate between deletes leaks a copy); no checkpoint while it is down. Growth tests assert used blocks each cycle.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261021T211831Z-daa0544e233ebf48","text":"Growth test asserts used blocks or a high-water of one index over the start, every cycle. No checkpoint while the HNSW index is down; the next cycle reclaims that free copy. Operator 2026-10-21.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261021T213401Z-eb3da00d50779e55","text":"HNSW stays down until every embedding delete in the process has run, then one recreate. A recreate between two deletes leaks a used copy on DuckDB 1.5.4 and 2.0.0. Operator 2026-10-21.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
